Bonney's plot:{
Bonney's mother died when she was born due to illness and left her in the care of her beloved, Kuma. Kuma is a half-giant who raised Bonney as if he were her father. Until one day Bonney experienced the symptoms of the disease that killed her mother; Kuma, desperate for not knowing how to cure her, decided to let the world government along with the scientist Vega Punck experiment on his body in exchange for curing Bonney. The girl was not aware of this, it was not until she was cured by Vega Punck that she learned that her father had been transformed into a cyborg with no feelings or memories. Bonney, who is only 10 years old, decides to go out to sea to rescue her father, using the power of her fruit to pose as an adult to recruit a crew and go to Egg Head, the island of the future, where her father was. Even along the way she has experienced things that a girl should never experience, from seeing her crew being slaughtered by other pirates, to almost being enslaved herself. Still, in spite of all her love for his father, it prevents her from giving up and even without a crew, she strives to one day be able to see him again. Life as a pirate is very hard, so she had to adopt an aggressive personality so as not to appear helpless, but deep down she is still a scared little girl who just wants to see her father again.
}
